##	Worldbuilding

§1.1 Magic Rules (Summary & Additions)

  * Due to the Mantles healing witnessed wounds, military women need to use Mantles of other military women who would have known wounds of the fetus. This is the only way to heal a damaged pregnancy while remaining on the battlefield. A warrior woman relying on a male Mantle while pregnant runs a significant risk of losing her child, and so over the ages that practice would be seldom seen. They would always need at least one secondary woman Mantle that they would wield exclusively while pregnant. As such, most young girls are encouraged to learn their first military Mantle from a woman ancestor, and only on their second choice may they branch out to a man's. This could have been a glaring flaw with the 1rst son, who likely had a male military Mantle and struggled to make the shift to Aveline's Huntress mantle. Gwion, having been taught to respect the Huntress early by his sister, sidesteps this issue entirely. Men don't face the same issue, though it could be a funny annecdote or urban legend of a soldier using a woman's Mantle and losing his genitals in a stroke of bad luck on the battlefield, them not regenerating afterwards.

